### Finite-difference slab

A 1D slab: indices `i : Fin (n+1)` or `i ∈ Finset.range (n+1)`, with functions `u, v : ℤ → ℝ` or `Fin (n+1) → ℝ`. Forward difference `Δ⁺ u i = u (i+1) - u i`, backward difference `Δ⁻ u i = u i - u (i-1)`.

Summation by parts on `i = 0..n-1`:
`∑_{i=0}^{n-1} u_i (v_{i+1} - v_i) = [u_n v_n - u_0 v_0] - ∑_{i=0}^{n-1} (u_{i+1} - u_i) v_{i+1}`.

Wait let me derive. Let `Δ⁺ v_i = v_{i+1} - v_i`. Then
`∑_{i=0}^{n-1} u_i Δ⁺v_i = ∑ u_i v_{i+1} - ∑ u_i v_i`.
Reindex first sum `j = i+1`: `∑_{j=1}^{n} u_{j-1} v_j`. So
= `∑_{j=1}^{n} u_{j-1} v_j - ∑_{j=0}^{n-1} u_j v_j`
= `u_{n-1} v_n - u_0 v_0 + ∑_{j=1}^{n-1} (u_{j-1} - u_j) v_j`
= `u_{n-1} v_n - u_0 v_0 - ∑_{j=1}^{n-1} (Δ⁺u_{j-1}) v_j`.

With vanishing boundary terms (`u_0 = 0` and `v_n = 0`), we get
`∑_{i=0}^{n-1} u_i (v_{i+1} - v_i) = -∑_{i=0}^{n-1} (u_{i+1} - u_i) v_{i+1}`
or equivalently with `w_i = v_{i+1}`:
`∑ u_i (w_i - v_i) = -∑ (u_{i+1} - u_i) w_i` when `u_0 = 0`, `w_{n-1} = 0`.

Hmm. This is a 1D slab. The task says "finite-difference slab", which could be a multidimensional box. But 1D is a slab (an interval) with vanishing boundary terms. Maybe make it slightly more general: a slab in one direction with arbitrary "transverse" index, i.e., `α × Fin (n+1)`: `u, v : α → Fin (n+1) → ℝ` with a finite type α. Then sum over α and the slab. Boundary terms are at i=0 and i=n. This is closer to a slab (product of a cross-section with an interval) and is still easily provable with `Finset.sum_comm`/`Finset.sum_product`.

