Proof using `Fin.sum_univ_succ` and `Fin.sum_univ_castSucc`:
```lean
lemma sum_forwardDiff_telescope {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G] (g : Fin (n+1) → G) :
    ∑ i : Fin n, (g i.succ - g i.castSucc) = g (Fin.last n) - g 0 := by
  have h1 : ∑ i : Fin n, g i.succ = (∑ i : Fin (n+1), g i) - g 0 := by
    rw [Fin.sum_univ_succ]
    abel
  have h2 : ∑ i : Fin n, g i.castSucc = (∑ i : Fin (n+1), g i) - g (Fin.last n) := by
    rw [Fin.sum_univ_castSucc]
    abel
  rw [Finset.sum_sub_distrib, h1, h2]
  abel
```

Wait, `Fin.sum_univ_succ` gives `∑ i : Fin (n+1), g i = g 0 + ∑ i : Fin n, g i.succ`. So `∑ i : Fin n, g i.succ = ∑ i : Fin (n+1), g i - g 0`. With `abel` after `rw [Fin.sum_univ_succ]`? Let's see: goal `∑ i : Fin n, g i.succ = ∑ i, g i - g 0`. `rw [Fin.sum_univ_succ]` rewrites `∑ i, g i` on RHS to `g 0 + ∑ i : Fin n, g i.succ`. Then goal: `∑ i, g i.succ = (g 0 + ∑ i, g i.succ) - g 0`. `abel` closes. Good. Similarly for castSucc: `Fin.sum_univ_castSucc` gives `∑ i, g i = (∑ i : Fin n, g i.castSucc) + g (last n)`. Then RHS = `(∑ i, g i.castSucc) + g last - g last`; `abel` closes.

